hello and welcome to med simplified  diabetes is nothing less than a pandemic  in 2003 194 million people suffer from  diabetes and by 2025  this number is projected to increase by  72 percent  to  333 million  in 2016 an estimated 1.6 million deaths  were directly caused by diabetes which  makes diabetes the seventh leading cause  of death in 2016.  diabetes affects persons of all ages and  races the disease reduces both a  person's quality of life and life  expectancy and imposes a large economic  burden on the health care system and on  the families  diabetes is a metabolic disease  characterized by hyperglycemia which is  excessive concentration of glucose in  your blood this is due to a defect in  the beta cells of your pancreas which  secrete insulin or it can be a defect at  the cellular level which the receptors  can have and they do not react properly  to the insulin  this persistently high sugar in the  blood affects virtually every organ in  your body and it leads to various  problems like heart attacks strokes  irreversible nerve damage ulcers that  don't heal severe infections retinal  damage leading to permanent blindness  and kidney failure  a pregnant female with diabetes is at an  increased risk of abortions and serious  complications  now your diet plays an important role in  managing diabetes one reason is that the  food you eat on a day to day basis has a  direct impact on your blood sugar levels  for instance high carb foods raise your  blood sugar levels the digestive system  breaks down the digestible ones into  sugar which enters a blood but then  again not all carbohydrates are bad  complex carbohydrates like whole grains  take longer to digest while simple carbs  like white flour and refined sugars may  cause sudden spikes in your blood sugar  levels  indian foods are deeply rooted in  history and are probably one of the  oldest foods known to mankind  traditional indian foods are extremely  diverse just as its geography many  stable foods species and vegetables in  the indian diet are very good for people  with diabetes  so in this video we will be discussing  five such traditional indian foods that  have been scientifically proven to have  health benefits for people suffering  from diabetes  number one barley  a study done by a university in sweden  states that eating a special mixture of  dietary fibers found in barley can help  reduce your appetite as well as high  blood sugar levels  whole grains like oats brown rice or  millets like jar or ragi contain both  soluble and insoluble fiber that helps  with sugar control number 2 bitter guard  also known as karela  bitter guard contains an insulin-like  compound called polypeptide p or p  insulin which has been shown to control  diabetes naturally a report issued in  the journal of chemistry and biology  gives evidence that consumption of  bitter guard tends to increase the  uptake of glucose in the cells and  improves glycemic control  number three amla also known as  gooseberry  amla also known as indian gooseberry is  a traditional remedy to control high  blood sugar levels it also contains the  mineral chromium which regulates  carbohydrate metabolism and helps in  making your body more responsive to  insulin  number four fenugreek also known as  methi  a study published in the international  journal of vitamin and nutrition  research found that a daily dose of 10  grams of fenugreek seeds soaked in hot  water helps to control type 2 diabetes  fenugreek water has the ability to lower  blood sugar in people with diabetes it  contains fiber and helps in slowing down  the digestion process further regulating  the absorption of carbohydrates and  sugar  the fenugreek water also helps in  improving the way your body uses sugar  the number five and the last food that  we have are beans  beans contain a healthy dose of fiber  nutrients and protein keeping us full  for a longer time and reducing our  carbohydrate intake a low glycemic index  effectively reduces blood sugar level  beans are an excellent source of  vegetable protein and are extremely  beneficial for diabetics a cup of beans  or lentils each day combined with a low  glycemic diet was shown to lower blood  sugar levels and coronary artery risk  disease in patients with type 2 diabetes  so friends these were the 5 best types  of foods that you should include in your  diet if you have diabetes make sure to  subscribe to our channel so that you  don't miss out on our upcoming videos  about diabetes health we will discuss  about the precautions you should take if  you have diabetes best types of  exercises for people with diabetes and  much more  i hope you found this video helpful if  you did make sure to hit the like button  below to support us you can also support  me simplified by clicking the join  button below or joining our page at  patreon.com thank you so much for  watching see you in the next video
 

